From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tgmeinde <tgmeinde@amd.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 14:10:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] so_arm101: accept a trajectory that is still moving

MoveIt Servo streams a joint trajectory whose last point still carries the
joint speed. The trajectory controller drops any such message, so the arm
only follows the occasional point whose end speed is zero and then runs past
the joint speed limit. Servo is the stream this controller has to accept.

---

diff --git a/so_arm101_description/control/ros2_controllers.yaml b/so_arm101_description/control/ros2_controllers.yaml
index 57de2a4..b7c4e1a 100644
--- a/so_arm101_description/control/ros2_controllers.yaml
+++ b/so_arm101_description/control/ros2_controllers.yaml
@@ -35,6 +35,10 @@ joint_trajectory_controller:
       - <robot_namespace>elbow_flex_joint
       - <robot_namespace>wrist_flex_joint
       - <robot_namespace>wrist_roll_joint
+    # Servo streams a trajectory whose last point still carries the joint speed.
+    # The controller drops that trajectory unless this is set, and the arm then
+    # only moves on the few points whose end speed is zero.
+    allow_nonzero_velocity_at_trajectory_end: true
     # A goal tolerance of 0 disables the check, so a move that is still short
     # is reported as success. 0.01 rad is the start tolerance MoveIt already
     # uses. goal_time 0 waits until the arm is there.
